DESCRIPTION:Image: Rupy C. Tut\, (detail) Beeji da Ghar (My Grandmother’
 s Home)\, 2023 (Photo by Phillip Maisel)Join us for an artist panel and ce
 lebration for the exhibition\, What We Carry\, featuring artists Al-An deS
 ouza\, Angela Hennessy\, Stephanie Syjuco\, Rupy C. Tut\, and Maryam Yousi
 f.\nFive Bay Area artists explore questions of inheritance from those who 
 came before us–in our bodies\, in our materials\, and in our shared reco
 rd–and what we make of what we choose to keep.\nWhat We Carry is on view
  in Thacher Gallery from December 3\, 2026–February 14\, 2027\, closed f
 rom Dec. 24-Jan.3. Presented by the MA in Museum Studies program in collab
 oration with guest curator and instructor Deena Chalabi.\n\nLocated in USF
 ’s Gleeson Library-Geschke Center\, the Thacher Gallery is free and open
  to the public from noon to 6 pm daily at 2130 Fulton Street. usfca.edu/th
 acher-gallery\nHoliday hours.\n\nImage: Rupy C. Tut\, (detail) Beeji da Gh
 ar (My Grandmother’s Home)\, 2023 (Photo by Phillip Maisel)\n\nFree\n\nT
 ickets: https://www.usfca.edu/event/what-we-carry-artist-panel/13663273\nD
 etails: https://sf.funcheap.com/carry-free-artist-panel-5-bay-area-artists
 -usf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
